# Fixture: Ubuntu 22.04+ RFC3339 auth.log format.
#
# Lines whose program is `sshd` are SYNTHETIC. This development machine is WSL2
# with no openssh-server installed, so not one real sshd line exists anywhere on
# it. The message bodies below are taken from the OpenSSH 9.x catalogue encoded
# in /etc/fail2ban/filter.d/sshd.conf, which is the authoritative list of what
# sshd actually emits and is what fail2ban itself matches against in production.
#
# Every other line (sudo, login, systemd-logind, CRON, (systemd)) is REAL and
# was copied verbatim out of this box's /var/log/auth.log. Those are what keep
# the prefix regex honest about the shapes it has to survive: a missing pid
# bracket, a parenthesised program name, and a hyphenated one.
#
# Comment lines and blank lines are here on purpose too — the parser must skip
# them rather than raise.

